From 296951facddc008333459aba153da9c04f881f95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:03:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 002/371] pirates: ships - deployer, deploy ring, first ship,
 task leak (Sept 2026 family-server fixes)

- DistributedShipDeployerAI: rewritten deploy flow. A deployed ship launches
  at the free berth nearest the dinghy the pirate used, is kept in position by
  the AI until a client takes the wheel (no more ships sitting at the ocean
  origin inside the island), and is invulnerable for a short spawn window.
- ClientAreaBuilderAI, DistributedIslandAI: measure the deploy radii off each
  island's own shoreline (moored dinghies, port blocker) so berths sit on the
  water instead of on the far LOD sphere.
- DistributedShipDeployer (client): deploy barrier is a vertical tube so it
  only pushes a ship sideways, and the reef warning shows once, not per frame.
- DistributedShipAI, GameFSMShipAI, NPCShipAI, ShipManagerAI: stop the
  broadcast-pos / path-follow tasks when a ship is deleted (ai.log assertion
  leak), wash a sunk player ship's crew ashore before deleting it, add the
  missing hasActiveShip, spawn NPC enemy ships in open water away from
  islands and players, and only count explicit flagship spawns as flagships.
- PirateInventoryAI: a new pirate with no ship gets a light sloop (the
  tutorial is skipped), and one with no quests gets the Chapter 2 opener.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
